    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 the only test class passes. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the soft-duplicate (\"possible duplicate\") flag for owners.\n\n**What \"possible duplicate\" means:** an owner that isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a *different* telephone. (A shared last name + postcode with a *matching* telephone would be a hard duplicate, already rejected with 409 at create by `RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity`, so a differing telephone is exactly the soft-match case.)\n\n**Changes (kept structurally small):**\n1. **`PossibleDuplicate.java`** (new, self-contained helper, mirrors the existing `NamesakeCount` pattern) \u2014 scans owners, returns the matching owner's id (lowest when several match) or `null`. Owners without a postcode never soft-match.\n2. **`RespondWithOwner.java`** (GET responder) \u2014 3 lines: set `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` on the DTO.\n3. **`RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`** (POST responder) \u2014 same 3 lines, so the create response is faithful to the spec too.\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the two read-only fields to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` has the setters.\n\nEach touched method stays complexity-1 with essentially no surrounding class complexity, and all the real logic lives in the new cohesive helper class rather than growing an existing one.\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
